-- ============================================================================
-- PD5 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Gas Well Performance, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE DROPLET BALANCE AT ONE POINT, and that point is the
-- WELLHEAD, because that is the gauge an operator reads. A gas well loads up
-- when the gas can no longer carry the liquid it is producing, and the whole
-- of the classical treatment is a force balance on a single droplet: drag
-- against weight, a terminal velocity, a flow area, and one ratio that
-- decides. Every number in this tier comes out of a gas density, a terminal
-- velocity or a single-station loading check.
--
-- THE TIER ENDS ON A CONCLUSION THAT IS WRONG, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Read at
-- the wellhead the capstone well is comfortably unloaded, at a ratio of
-- 1.2552, and it still passes there under the stricter correlation. It is
-- nonetheless loading over the bottom third of its string. A learner who
-- finishes this tier can compute everything an operator reads off a surface
-- gauge and will reach the wrong verdict from it, which is the strongest
-- possible motivation for the tier above.
--
-- TWO THINGS THE TIER MUST NOT ASSUME, and both are ways of quietly importing
-- a number instead of computing one.
--
--   THE Z FACTOR IS NOT 0.9. The published fixture hands the loading module a
--   FLAT 0.9 at every pressure from 300 to 2,500 psia, which is fine for an
--   oracle checking droplet algebra and wrong for a well whose pressure
--   triples down the string. This course takes z from the package's own
--   natural gas correlation, and on the capstone well it runs 0.8436 to
--   0.8677. Since z sits in the denominator of both the gas density and the
--   actual velocity, assuming one instead of computing one moves most of the
--   tier's answers.
--
--   AND THE TWO MODULES IN THE CHAIN DO NOT SPEAK THE SAME UNITS. The loading
--   module takes degR and the properties module takes degF, so the conversion
--   has to happen at the DOOR, with the package's own converter, rather than
--   as a hand-typed 459.67 somewhere in the middle. They also carry two
--   different molecular weights of air, 28.9647 and 28.9625, against the same
--   gas constant, so one gas density computed two ways differs by 76 parts per
--   million. Neither is a defect. Both are seams, and a seam is where a course
--   has to say which side it is standing on.
--
-- A RESULT WORTH STATING BECAUSE INTUITION GETS IT BACKWARDS. The HEAVIER
-- liquid makes the FASTER droplet. Brine is harder to lift than condensate,
-- and its terminal velocity is higher, because the terminal velocity rises
-- with the density difference and the brine's extra weight more than pays for
-- its higher surface tension. A tier that leaves a learner thinking the
-- lighter liquid falls faster has taught the balance backwards.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the well's own
-- stated conditions. The tier above restates every one of them from scratch.
-- ============================================================================

values ('gaswell', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-well-that-drowns","title":"A Well That Drowns","lesson_keys":["l01-why-a-gas-well-loads-up","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-the-droplet-picture"]},{"key":"m02-gas-at-a-station","title":"Gas at a Station","lesson_keys":["l01-z-at-pressure-and-temperature","l02-gas-density","l03-what-density-decides","l04-reading-one-station","l05-what-one-station-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m03-the-droplet-balance","title":"The Droplet Balance","lesson_keys":["l01-drag-against-weight","l02-terminal-velocity","l03-surface-tension-and-density","l04-brine-against-condensate","l05-what-the-balance-assumes"]},{"key":"m04-critical-velocity-and-rate","title":"Critical Velocity and Rate","lesson_keys":["l01-from-velocity-to-rate","l02-flow-area","l03-the-critical-rate","l04-the-actual-velocity","l05-the-ratio-that-decides"]},{"key":"m05-two-correlations","title":"Two Correlations","lesson_keys":["l01-turner-and-coleman","l02-the-twenty-percent","l03-which-one-and-where","l04-what-a-correlation-is-not"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
